  "cues": [
   [
    0.1,
    "You met the chain in chapter two: amino acids joined by peptide links, with a free amino end, the N-terminal, and a free carboxyl end, the C-terminal."
   ],
   [
    9.816,
    "But a freshly made chain is not yet a working protein."
   ],
   [
    13.045,
    "Protein folding is the process by which a polypeptide chain folds into its biologically active shape, called the native three-dimensional structure."
   ],
   [
    21.717,
    "Shape matters, because the structure of a protein is crucial to its function."
   ],
   [
    26.118,
    "A folded protein has a pocket that fits its partner."
   ],
   [
    29.334,
    "Unfold it, or fold it wrongly, and the partner no longer fits."
   ],
   [
    33.826,
    "And different sequences of amino acids fold into different shapes."
   ],
   [
    37.889,
    "Every side chain is a different brick, and the order of the bricks decides where the chain bends."
   ]
  ]
